    "use": "POST JSON {action, nonce, signature, vaultAddress?, expiresAfter?}. Actions: order, cancel, cancelByCloid, scheduleCancel, modify, batchModify, updateLeverage, updateIsolatedMargin, usdSend, spotSend, sendAsset, withdraw3, usdClassTransfer, vaultTransfer, cDeposit/cWithdraw, tokenDelegate, approveAgent, approveBuilderFee, twapOrder, twapCancel. Order fields: a (asset index: perp = index in meta.universe, spot = 10000 + spotMeta index), b (isBuy), p (price string), s (size string), r (reduceOnly), t ({limit:{tif:Alo|Ioc|Gtc}} or {trigger:{isMarket,triggerPx,tpsl:tp|sl}}), c (optional 128-bit hex cloid); grouping na|normalTpsl|positionTpsl. Nonce = current ms timestamp. Signing: two schemes. (1) L1 actions (order, cancel, modify, leverage...): keccak256(msgpack(action) || nonce as 8-byte BE || 0x00 or 0x01+vaultAddress || optional 0x00+expiresAfter 8-byte BE) = connectionId; sign EIP-712 'Agent' {source: 'a' mainnet / 'b' testnet, connectionId: bytes32} with domain {name:'Exchange', version:'1', chainId:1337, verifyingContract:0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000}. (2) User-signed actions (usdSend, spotSend, withdraw3, usdClassTransfer, approveAgent, approveBuilderFee...): EIP-712 over the action itself with domain {name:'HyperliquidSignTransaction', version:'1', chainId: action.signatureChainId (SDK uses 0x66eee), verifyingContract: zero address} and hyperliquidChain 'Mainnet'|'Testnet'. Official docs strongly recommend using an SDK (msgpack field order, trailing zeros and lowercase addresses all break signatures). Testnet: https://api.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/exchange.",
